Havoc-OS
===========

Getting started
---------------

To get started with Android/Havoc-OS, you'll need to get familiar with [Source Control Tools](https://source.android.com/setup/develop).

To initialize your local repository using the Havoc-OS trees, use a command like this:
```
repo init -u https://github.com/havoc-OOS/android.git -b havoc-1.0 --git-lfs
```
Then to sync up:
```
repo sync
```
Please see the [Havoc-OS Wiki](https://wiki.havoc-os.com/) for building instructions, by device.


Submitting patches
------------------
Patches are always welcome! Please submit your patches via Havoc-OS Gerrit!

Simply follow our guide on [how to submit patches](https://wiki.havoc-os.com/submitting-patch-howto.html).

To view the status of your and others' patches, visit [Havoc-OS Gerrit Code Review](https://gerrit.havoc-os.com/).


Buildbot
--------

All supported devices are built weekly and periodically as changes are committed to ensure the source trees remain buildable.

You can view the current build statuses at [Havoc-OS Buildkite](https://buildkite.com/havoc-os).

Builds produced weekly by the buildbot can be downloaded from [Havoc-OS downloads](https://download.havoc-os.com/).
